# Units of work declared by scripts/03-verify-components.sh.
#
# Each id must record exactly one gate_unit_ran (with a measured quantity) or
# gate_unit_skipped (with a reason) before the script reaches gate_end. The old
# "(16 checks)" summary counted `CHECKS=$((CHECKS + 1))` statements in the source
# text, all of which sat at column 0 outside every guard — so the number was a
# constant of the file and stayed 16 whether a check ran or self-skipped.
#
# `xcode-regression` is the unit whose silent success started this: it was the
# most expensive slice in the gate and emitted nothing at all on the RAN path.

shell-compat
version-json
cli-syntax
terminal-prereqs
native-helper-sources
lua-plugin-syntax
yazi-flavor-assets
yazi-launch-surface
removed-gh-guard
regression-tests
xcode-regression
privileged-surface
non-concurrency-allowlist
weather-removal-guard
theme-manifest
view-modifier-lint
overlay-recurrence
